    "configuration": "The 2/2 study uses generated normalized CFG. The 3/3 study uses the published raw CFG with only its invariant changed from H_CandidatesOrLeadersVotedForSelf to the graph target and CHECK_DEADLOCK FALSE appended. Source and all action definitions are unchanged. Input identities in the rows bind actual CFG bytes and resolved IR.",
    "claim": "Every original initial state is covered. Every raw action successor satisfies definedness and the target, including destinations crossing the original constraint. All successors within term/log bounds also preserve typed representation and all 29 strengthening predicates. Dropping only the four channel cardinality conjuncts proves a stronger property. No bound on execution length. Counts are symbolic obligations, not reachable states."
  },
  "encoding": "Each of four membership predicates is keyed by the entire typed record including a canonical payload. Set insertion/deletion changes only the matching key. Other records retain their prestate membership. Negated obligations are Skolemized, then universally quantified assumptions may be weakened to selected full-key instances. Only UNSAT discharges an obligation.",
